# Evaluation outputs.
#
# A full sweep is a few hundred MB per policy, almost all of it charts and
# per-step time series. None of it is tracked: a results tree is reproducible
# by re-running evaluate.py, and keeping one in the repo would make the clone
# large for no benefit.
#
# If you want to keep a sweep, keep reward_components.csv. Cost and carbon are
# deterministic functions of the timestamp and linear in the energy rate, so
# that one file lets a different normalisation be scored without re-simulating
# anything.
results/
smart_buildings/results/

# Holdout data must never enter this repo. These rules are a backstop in case a
# generator is ever pointed at the default output path.
smart_buildings/test_buildings/
smart_buildings/test_scenarios/
**/holdout*/
**/test_set*/

# Climate.OneBuilding weather work dir (hvac_controller/weather.py).
weather_tmyx/

# The 30 shipped scenarios (~100 MB of .npy). Rebuilt exactly by
# `python -m smart_buildings.run_scenario_generator`; also in the Kaggle competition data.
smart_buildings/training_scenarios/
